# THE MOMENT A COLOSSUS'S FOOT COMES DOWN NEARBY (19_colossi `_landed`,
# colossus_foot.gd `land`). The straddling walker is staged ten world minutes
# before its foot comes down in this world's first tread, and the player stands
# outside one of its craters, facing the pad's place, the view tipped up: the pad
# comes down out of the sky over the last hundred metres, the slowest part of
# the whole step, and lands. The ground shakes at once (it is a few hundred
# metres off), a wall of dust rolls out off every pad, steam vents from the
# drum's joints, and the shock goes out through everything that sways. The
# pads stop bodies from three hundred metres up (`colossus_blocks`).
#   TOUR_TIMEOUT=400 tools/tour.sh tours/colossi_landing.tour --seed=7 --place=tread0 --colossus=2@tread0-10 --hour=12 --view=shoulder --weather=clear:0
await colossus_foot 30
near colossus_pad
mouse 0,-100 0.5
wait 1
shot 00-coming-down
until colossus_blocks 20
shot 01-over-the-crater
until colossus_tread 30
shot 02-down
wait 0.4
shot 03-the-dust-goes-out
wait 1
shot 04-the-dust-goes-out
wait 2
shot 05-the-dust-goes-out
wait 4
shot 06-settling
wait 6
shot 07-settled
